# Design library

## AI4R M2a research runtime proposal

[[Designs/ai4r_m2a/README|ai4r_m2a]] defines adaptive, long-running research on JiuwenSwarm with portable category capsules, enforced checks, durable evidence and reproducible artifacts. Read its five Level 1 views first. Core behavior is independent of the current code diff; the separate conversion guide maps the inspected implementation. This proposed runtime design can use the selected lab infrastructure; it does not replace that infrastructure design or retroactively amend M1. Runtime acceptance remains NOT_RUN.


[[Designs/Lab Design Comparison|Checkpoint 1: compare the lab designs]] precedes the next architecture selection. The user subsequently selected VM per lab and selective JiuwenBox reuse. [[Designs/Sandbox Lab Design]] owns checkpoint 2; the deck has not yet been reconciled.

**Current M2 sandbox route:** [[Designs/Sandbox Lab Design]] → [seven-view diagram set](Sandbox%20Lab%20Diagrams/README.md) → [[Designs/M2 Lab Capsules and Factory Proposal]]. This route supersedes conflicting details in the earlier VM/container/factory drafts for proposal discussion; the replacement [[Designs/Lab Capsule and Factory Design Plan|delivery plan]] prioritizes evidence-driven research adaptation before infrastructure expansion. Implementation agreements remain open.

## Start with the current overview

[[Designs/Labs and Capability Capsules]] is the concise component view for application developers. [[Resources/Artifact Library]] holds actual documents and reference copies; [[Presentation Library/Deck Catalog]] indexes actual decks. Use this index for detailed designs and historical lineage. The October 23 M2 handoff below is a proposed implementation route, not a requirement to adopt its topology in every lab.

## Latest M2 handoff and source update

[[Resources/Handoffs/m2-labs/README|M2 implementation handoffs]] is the portable implementation package for VM labs, container capsules and local factories. Shared identity/protocol/resource/admission contracts and acceptance scenarios are included; existing design notes retain the full target and provenance.


**Current notebook reading package:** [[Designs/CC History]] · [[Designs/Project Authority]] · [[Designs/CC Reference]] · [[Designs/Lab Progression]] · [[Amendments/README]]. [[Resources/Current Baseline]] distinguishes the maintained design checkout from captured M1 implementation snapshots.

[[Presentation Library/README|Presentation Library]] collects recurring talk, evidence, visual-density and review guidance. See [[Presentation Library/Preference and Source Register]] for what was directly requested, what is found in project source files, and the limits of the chat search.

Design is a first-class part of this notebook. This index connects current contracts, research proposals, previous designs, diagrams, and presentations without creating a second maintained copy of the product architecture.

